  "guide": {"focus":"Watch how the rods keep their lengths as motion and forces pass along the chain.","predict":{"prompt":"With weaker gravity, how does the chain's swing period change?","options":["It becomes longer","It becomes shorter","It is unchanged"]},"variables":[{"control":"world.gravity.strength","label":"Gravity strength"}],"steps":[{"text":"Run once, then select a rod to see the force it carries."},{"text":"Reduce gravity, press R, and run the same interval.","control":"world.gravity.strength"},{"text":"Compare the chain's motion with the previous run.","open":"measure.graph"}],"expect":"The rods preserve their lengths while forces pass through the mechanism. Weaker gravity produces slower swinging and smaller support reactions.","limits":"The rods have no mass and are treated as perfectly rigid. The iterative solver allows a small error, especially in very stiff connected systems."},
